From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoCo starter <coco-starter@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:59:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] machine: keep the configured frame skip without a rate
 limit

Turning the rate limit off normally forces a ten-frame skip on the
Dragon/CoCo 1/2 and CoCo 3 machines. Rendered-frame capture needs every
frame, so keep the frame skip that -fskip configured instead.

This is test equipment for the CoCo starter's scripts/coco.py.
---
 src/coco3.c         | 2 +-
 src/dragon/dragon.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/coco3.c b/src/coco3.c
index 02fec83a8f47e7d02b8640ecb240049c61bcbbb2..45ee3372be42ed7b5fecf098818ed33c2cfeee77 100644
--- a/src/coco3.c
+++ b/src/coco3.c
@@ -1076,7 +1076,7 @@ static void coco3_ui_set_ratelimit(void *sptr, int tag, void *smsg) {
 	if (uimsg->value) {
 		mp->frameskip = mp->configured_frameskip;
 	} else {
-		mp->frameskip = 10;
+		mp->frameskip = mp->configured_frameskip;
 	}
 }
 
diff --git a/src/dragon/dragon.c b/src/dragon/dragon.c
index 98375cd2c219739ff732ce3ed393b64afa83bfd5..0c04f7a1de854ff01d2f9f6f2d5d51e12b72b4ce 100644
--- a/src/dragon/dragon.c
+++ b/src/dragon/dragon.c
@@ -1013,7 +1013,7 @@ static void dragon_ui_set_ratelimit(void *sptr, int tag, void *smsg) {
 	if (uimsg->value) {
 		md->frameskip = md->configured_frameskip;
 	} else {
-		md->frameskip = 10;
+		md->frameskip = md->configured_frameskip;
 	}
 }
 
